==English==

===Etymology===
The keyword ''new'' creates an object in [[C++]] and derived languages.

===Verb===
{{en-verb|*}}

# {{lb|en|programming|informal|transitive}} To create (an [[object]]) by calling its [[constructor]].
#: {{synonyms|en|new}}
#* {{quote-book|en|year=2000|author=Robert C. Martin|title=More C++ gems
|passage=If an exception occurs trying to '''new up''' bar1 or bar2, the TFoo part of the object won't have changed {{...}}}}
#* {{quote-newsgroup|en|year=2003|author=Jonathan Hoyle|title=Pointers?|newsgroup=comp.lang.basic.realbasic
|passage=So you just '''new up''' the object you want and once its internal reference count drops to 0, the language deletes it (during a free time as a background thread).}}
